# dialface
#
# Figures only, tall and narrow, for scale plates and dial rings. A pressure
# gauge scale wants 0 to 160 round a 40 mm circle in twelve places, and
# panelgothic figures at a legible height will not go round it. These are the
# same height and two thirds the width.
#
# Same grid as panelgothic: 1000 to the em, capitals at 700, and the same
# 80 unit side bearing rule so the two faces can be mixed on one plate
# without the spacing jumping.
#
# There are no letters in it and there is not going to be. A scale that
# needs a word on it sets the word in panelgothic; a numeric face with a
# half drawn alphabet in it is a face somebody will use for a legend.

face dialface
upem 1000
cap 700
xheight 500
ascender 750
descender -200
linegap 100

glyph space 240 U+0020

glyph plus 380 U+002B
  s 190,470 190,170
  s 90,320 290,320

glyph comma 260 U+002C
  s 155,90 155,10 130,-60 90,-110

glyph hyphen 380 U+002D
  s 90,320 290,320

glyph period 280 U+002E
  s 190,60 190,0

glyph slash 380 U+002F
  s 90,-60 290,760

glyph zero 360 U+0030
  s 190,700 140,680 110,610 100,500 100,200 110,90 140,20 190,0 240,20 270,90 280,200 280,500 270,610 240,680 190,700

